ID: e1d56c28-8c6b-40d0-a9b2-a5e228d511a0
Comment: In `TestDefaultSNIWithPortMappingOnly`, the handler still responds with `body "hello from a.caddy.localhost"` but the assertion was changed to expect `"hello from a"`. This looks like a test mismatch that will fail even if the SNI behavior is correct.

ID: a7a3d433-7d1f-43b9-b8e1-5e610c3fe22c
Comment: The original code unconditionally assigned `cp.DefaultSNI = defaultSNI` to every TLS connection policy, regardless of whether the policy's hosts actually include or handle the default SNI. This could cause unintended routing or fallback behavior when `defaultSNI` differs from the explicit block hosts. Moving the assignment inside the `if h == defaultSNI` block ensures the field is only set on policies that explicitly manage the default SNI, correctly relying on the catch-all policy appended later in the function for general fallbacks.

ID: cc29afbd-efa4-48aa-ab3d-1d88bfc3949d
Comment: In `serversFromPairings`, `cp.DefaultSNI = defaultSNI` is now assigned inside the `for _, h := range hosts` loop when `h == defaultSNI`. Could we make this clearer by tracking a `matchedDefaultSNI` boolean in the loop, then assigning `cp.DefaultSNI` once after the loop? It would separate host scanning from policy mutation and make the control flow easier to read.

ID: 6dc44d71-bde7-4c39-a3bf-883cfb439c36
Comment: The line `cp.DefaultSNI = defaultSNI` was moved inside the `if h == defaultSNI` block, but it seems like it should still be set unconditionally outside this block. Does this change introduce a logic error where the default SNI is not set for all hosts?

ID: 2ecc89bb-07cb-4669-9541-c269711e72af
Comment: Appending `""` to `hosts` means `len(hosts) > 0`, so the `else` block that sets `hasCatchAllTLSConnPolicy = true` is skipped. This will cause a redundant catch-all `ConnectionPolicy` to be added at the end of the function. Consider setting `hasCatchAllTLSConnPolicy = true` when the catch-all matcher is appended to the host list.

ID: 30b77727-37e6-4f0f-93ca-050f25474b35
Comment: [Correctness] In the `len(hosts) == 0` path, `cp.DefaultSNI` is no longer assigned. That means a catch-all TLS connection policy (for example a `:9443` server block) will now be created without the configured `default_sni`, and the later fallback append is skipped because `hasCatchAllTLSConnPolicy` is true. Was the intent to keep `DefaultSNI` on catch-all policies too?

ID: 0d9b2c05-554b-4095-af0a-891e86012914
Comment: The assignment to `cp.DefaultSNI` is now placed inside the loop that checks `if h == defaultSNI`. Is this intentional? It seems to change the logic as it may cause `DefaultSNI` to not be set if `defaultSNI` matches any host after the first.

