ID: 88373364-b8f9-481a-ac31-50a80675f03d
Comment: It seems that the assertion 'ai_assert(numOffsets < 20 && perVertexOffset < 20);' has been removed, which previously limited the size of allocations and may prevent possible out-of-bounds errors.

ID: 009fc0b3-c6e8-4792-800f-114b822f0ea8
Comment: Using `vindex.reserve(numOffsets)` only allocates memory; it does not change the size of the vector. Since `vindex.size()` remains 0, the subsequent use of `vindex[offsets]` in the loop will result in out-of-bounds access and undefined behavior. You should use `vindex.resize(numOffsets)` or initialize it with `std::vector<size_t> vindex(numOffsets);` instead.

ID: 0a48e7a1-4b45-4c8e-b57b-3bcc92e849c3
Comment: Replace `vindex.reserve(numOffsets)` and subsequent `vindex[offsets] = ...` assignment with `vindex.push_back(...)` or `vindex.emplace_back(...)`. `std::vector::reserve()` only allocates raw memory without updating the container's logical size. Using `operator[]` on a vector with `size() == 0` is undefined behavior and will likely cause a runtime crash or memory corruption in this tight parsing loop.

ID: 0fc3942c-da95-4916-b0f2-fa761932a1ee
Comment: In the new `CopyVertex` implementation, the line `vindex[offsets] = indices[...]` is accessing `vindex` with `offsets` while the vector has been reserved but not resized. This can lead to undefined behavior if `offsets` exceeds the current vector size.

ID: c54f34e8-45d3-4113-ad28-d5ec93722733
Comment: The new `ReadPrimTriStrips` function has a hard-coded winding direction adjustment for odd-numbered primitives, starting with 1 (zero-based). This makes the code fragile and harder to maintain if the algorithm changes or if someone needs to support custom winding orders.

ID: c3773ceb-8d11-4052-a9c5-0dd49544f7ca
Comment: `vindex.reserve(numOffsets)` allocates capacity but leaves the vector size at zero, so `vindex[offsets] = ...` writes out of bounds and causes undefined behavior. Use `std::vector<size_t> vindex(numOffsets)` or append with `push_back`.

ID: bcf70f86-cf1e-4153-9b9c-5fa4e4c7c276
Comment: [Correctness] `vindex` is only `reserve()`d here, but the loop writes to `vindex[offsets]` without resizing it first. That leaves the vector empty and makes every access out of bounds; this should probably be `resize(numOffsets)` or direct `push_back` usage.

ID: 6b16cdfa-d1e5-4380-aaf2-8c0de734a494
Comment: The `CopyVertex` function is duplicated with slightly different logic in `ReadPrimTriStrips`. Consider consolidating this logic into `CopyVertex` and passing additional parameters as needed.

ID: 1399c026-7dcd-47c1-96fe-407d34b47307
Comment: In `CopyVertex`, `vindex` is changed from a fixed array to `std::vector<size_t>` with only `reserve(numOffsets)`, but then written via `vindex[offsets] = ...`. `reserve()` does not change size, so indexing is out-of-bounds/UB here. Please use `vindex.resize(numOffsets)` (or `push_back`) before indexed writes.

