ID: 9cc2bacb-e26e-4f35-80df-f728579d921a
Comment: The test `shouldLimitNumberOfResponsesToNodeDataRequests` now uses the 3-argument constructor, which applies the default `maxGetNodeData` limit of 384. Since the test only dispatches 3 hashes, the limit is never actually reached, which means the test no longer verifies that the server correctly limits responses. To properly test this, consider using the 7-argument constructor to set a small limit (e.g., 2) or dispatching enough items to exceed the default limit.

