Comment: The test `shouldLimitNumberOfResponsesToNodeDataRequests` verifies that exactly 2 responses are sent when 3 are requested. The patch replaces the explicit 7-argument constructor with the 3-argument convenience constructor, which internally uses `DEFAULT_MAX_GET_NODE_DATA` (384 as defined in `EthServer.java`). This changes the effective limit from 2 to 384, causing the test to return all 3 node data items and fail the `verify` assertion. The test should either explicitly pass a limit of 2 to the `maxGetNodeData` parameter, or update the expected list in the assertion to contain 3 values.

