ID: 9658b70b-e340-4c35-b8e5-5e9ca834d8da
Comment: The removal of the `_MSC_VER` check for the `O_BINARY` flag might introduce incorrect behavior when running on Windows platforms. Previously, this flag ensured the file was opened in binary mode, which is necessary for Windows compatibility. Are you certain that the removal of the binary mode is intended?

ID: 366fa647-2e8c-4cc4-ade0-583b25c1a664
Comment: Keep `O_BINARY` for the `_MSC_VER` path. On Windows, `open(filename, O_RDONLY)` uses text-mode translation by default; wrapping that descriptor in protobuf's `FileInputStream` can produce incorrect byte counts/content for CRLF or Ctrl-Z, causing otherwise valid prototxt files to parse incorrectly. Preserve the conditional `O_RDONLY | O_BINARY` behavior.

ID: 8be4a6bf-f55d-4f20-8977-e507ffb66d53
Comment: `ReadProtoFromTextFile()` no longer opens the file with `O_BINARY` on `_MSC_VER`. On Windows, text-mode translation can alter protobuf input bytes (especially `\r\n` handling), so this change may break parsing of `.prototxt` files on the very platform this PR is meant to support.

ID: 935290be-b08e-46f3-8c06-2bb962a79f38
Comment: In `ReadProtoFromTextFile` (`src/caffe/common.cpp`), removing `O_BINARY` under `_MSC_VER` changes Windows file-open semantics to text mode. Was this intentional? Text mode can translate bytes (e.g., `\r\n`, `0x1A` EOF handling), which may cause parse differences vs. non-Windows or previous behavior.

ID: 7d08719b-72d9-48b1-8b11-e9bb834aa177
Comment: The removal of the `_MSC_VER` conditional compilation for `O_BINARY` flag might cause issues on Windows platforms where binary mode is necessary for consistent file handling. This should be verified or reconsidered for Windows 7 64bit VS2012 compatibility.

ID: a2645a96-55bc-4a39-bb0d-9ac657422f00
Comment: Avoid adding `using std::string;` in a header file (`include/caffe/util/io.hpp`). This pollutes the `caffe` namespace for every file that includes this header, which can lead to name collisions.

ID: 027b0f24-b523-4d6b-98fb-b07a8548486a
Comment: The patch removes the `O_BINARY` flag for Windows (`_MSC_VER`). Given that the PR title indicates support for Windows, is there a reason for removing the platform-specific handling? Omitting `O_BINARY` on Windows may cause unexpected newline translations when reading text files.

