Comment: In `ControlConnection.java`, the `refreshNodeListAndTokenMap` method uses an existing pattern of collecting metadata in multiple parallel lists (`dseVersions`, `dseGraphEnabled`, `dseWorkloads`, etc.). Adding `hostIds` and `schemaVersions` to these parallel lists increases the fragility of this logic. This pattern is prone to errors during future maintenance; if any change to the row iteration or the population of these lists (e.g., adding a conditional check or a new field) causes the lists to become misaligned with `foundHosts`, metadata will be incorrectly assigned to the wrong hosts. It would be more robust to collect this data into a single metadata container object per row or to update the `Host` objects directly during the iteration if possible.

