Comment: The use of `Convert.ToDateTime(value)` changes the handling of `DBNull.Value`. The original code used a direct cast `(DateTime)value`, which would throw an `InvalidCastException` if the value was `DBNull.Value`. `Convert.ToDateTime(DBNull.Value)` returns `DateTime.MinValue`, meaning this method will now return `TimeSpan.Zero` for `NULL` database values instead of throwing an error. This silent conversion of a NULL to a valid value could lead to incorrect data being processed.

